{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>My wrong.</b> That my maidservant does — she does not wish to serve me." "<b>Upon you.</b> It is through you, for you do not protest on behalf of my honor, and I do not wish to afflict her since she coupled with you." "<b>May YHWH judge between me and you.</b> For I am mindful of your honor but you are not mindful of my honor." "<b>And between you.</b> Rashi explained: every ובינך in Scripture is defective, but this one is plene — read it וביניך — meaning, all the instances of ובינך are defective in their yod between the nun and the kaf, but this one is plene. <b>And between you.</b> All dotted words in the Torah were given to Ezra the Scribe. He said: if Moses our teacher comes and says to me, why did you write these? I say to him, I have already dotted them. And if he says to me, why did you dot them? I say to him, erase them and I will remove the dots from them. <b>We say in tractate Rosh HaShanah:</b> anyone who brings a complaint against his fellow is punished first, as Rashi explained here — that she brought the evil eye upon her account."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:25.424273230Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}